CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*invariant violation.*$
^.*lhs\.type\(\) == rhs\.type\(\).*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Regression for a convert_function return-type exception-safety crash.
Discarding the std::erase_if(...) result (vector::size_type) used to leave the
type-checker's `return_type` stale (set to size_type by the nested
convert_function of erase_if's body, whose throw was caught by the
system-header guard before the non-exception-safe restore ran).  main's
`return 0;` was then typed size_t while main's return slot stayed int, tripping
the symex invariant lhs.type() == rhs.type() (goto_symex.cpp) and aborting CBMC.
The fix restores `return_type` and the loop-context flags on every exit of
convert_function (N5008 [stmt.return]/3: `return` converts to the *enclosing*
function's return type).  The forbidden patterns guard against the crash's
return (invariant violation / the specific condition) and against a conversion
error.
